      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new transdermal beta-blocker containing system (Mepindolol BIO TSD) was compared in a placebo controlled cross over trial with a transdermal nitrate system in 14 patients suffering from coronary heart disease with stable angina pectoris. Under Mepindolol TSD both the incidence of angina pectoris attacks and the consumption of oral nitroglycerin dropped significantly. Under ergometry it resulted in an improvement in the maximum exercise tolerance and in a significant reduction in the ischemic ST-Segment deviation. Under Holter monitoring the number of manifest (MMI) and silent (SMI) ischemic episodes was significantly reduced. In addition the total duration of ischemia was significantly reduced. All the examined parameters showed Mepindolol BIO TSD to be significantly more effective than transdermal nitrate, and the duration of action was longer. No clinically relevant adverse events were observed in any of the therapeutic regimes."},
